	(gr_text_box "4 layers,\n2oz outer copper,\n1oz inner copper,\n1.67mm board thickness (not 1.6mm, as dielectric not readjusted when increasing outer copper width from 0.035mm to 0.07mm)\n\nPartition grounding scheme to separate high-power 'PGND' and logic 'GND'\n\nIn general, vias with solid, exposed copper (but via-in-pads must be plugged and filled)\n- On JLCPCB, select Epoxy Filled & Capped (POFV) or Via-in-Pad\n\n8 by 20 mil direct-connect, thermal vias\n\nNet class clearance and trace width values are all default since necking down will still throw DRC errors, so refer to pre-defined sizes and notes for actual minimums required"
		(start 139.7 12.7)
